quran[6]{c,v,t}:
  3,195,"Then, their Lord answered them: ‘Certainly I do not waste the work of any worker among you, whether male or female—one of you being from the other (i.e. each one of you is like the other, being on the same footing). So those who migrated or were expelled from their homes, and were persecuted in My way, and fought (in defence) and were killed, I shall surely acquit them of their misdeeds and shall admit them into the Gardens with flowing rivers beneath them, as a reward from Allah. And with Allah is the most beautiful reward."
  3,196,(O believer!) Let the bustle of the disbelievers in the towns not delude you.
  3,197,"(This is only) a brief enjoyment, then their abode will be the Hellfire. What an evil abode!"
  3,198,"But those who are conscious of their Lord shall have Gardens with rivers flowing beneath them. They will reside in them forever, as a hospitality that Allah Himself offers. And that which is with Allah is better for the virtuous."
  3,199,"Indeed, there are some among the People of the Book who truly believe in Allah, what has been revealed to you and what has been revealed to them. They humble themselves before Allah, never selling Allah’s revelations for a paltry gain. They shall have their reward with their Lord. Indeed, Allah is Swift in reckoning."
  3,200,"O believers! Be patient, excel in steadfastness, fortify your defence and be conscious of Allah, so that you may be successful."
